# issue #80's second instance. This fixture was originally handed over as a
# "healthy control" for chainrange.ofn; re-deriving the entailment showed
# Konclude reports C ⊑ D (via A ⊑ F, the same nested-existential monotonicity
# as nested-mono.ofn) and rustdl misses it — and that the chain and the range
# are BOTH irrelevant to the entailment, which is what led to filing #80 in
# the first place. So it is not a control at all.
#
# NOTE: this crate's own `build_model` REFUSES this fixture outright
# (Err(ChainRangeOutOfProfile)), so the acceptance invariant holds here
# trivially regardless of this oracle's content — recorded per the "one
# oracle per fixture" contract; see chainrange.oracle for the same caveat.
provenance: konclude-v0.7.0-1138
subclass: C D
